course: dictionary
lesson: 12502
title: Depiction: showing what something is like
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A depiction is a picture, description or performance that shows what someone or something is like. «The painting is a depiction of a king on his horse.» The painting shows the king, so it is the depiction.
explain: Authors use depictions too, in words. «The author's depiction of the lonely lighthouse keeper made me feel sad.» Lonely and sad are clues: the author is describing what the keeper is like, using words instead of paint.
explain: Depiction can also mean the act of showing something. Ask two questions: is it accurate, meaning true and correct, and is it realistic, meaning it looks like real life? A quick check is to swap in the words picture of or description of. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Depiction means a picture, description or performance that shows what someone or something is like.
fact: Depiction also means the act of showing something in art or words.
fact: «A depiction of» is always followed by the thing being shown, such as «a depiction of kings».
fact: «An accurate depiction» is a true, correct picture; «a realistic depiction» looks like real life.
fact: «The depiction of women» in a book or painting means how women are shown in it.
exercise: «The tapestry is a depiction of a battle.» What is a depiction? | A soldier's sword | A loud noise in the night | A kind of stone wall | *A picture or description that shows something
exercise: «Her book gives an accurate depiction of life in the village.» What does accurate depiction mean? | A made-up story with dragons | A map of the sea | A very short poem | *A true picture of how life really was
exercise: Ella says a depiction is only a photo. Why might she be wrong? | *A depiction can be a painting, a description in a book or a play | A depiction is a kind of food | A depiction is always a photo taken with a camera | A depiction is a loud sound
test: «The author's depiction of the hero made her seem very brave.» What does depiction mean here? | *The way the author shows the hero in words | A kind of dance | A long journey | A small hole in the wall
test: Which phrase means a true and correct picture of something? | A noisy depiction | *An accurate depiction | A sleepy depiction | A late depiction
exam: «The museum's new painting is a realistic depiction of everyday life in old London.» What does realistic suggest? | It has no colours at all | It is about aliens from space | It is very short | *It looks like real life
